    "about": "A wizard's hands in the Hold (the-hold.md, phase 3, World.Hands.cs). A hand is a slot: start says what each holds at first, an element or empty. The button is the gesture, thrust or throw, and both on one hand a sweep, and what the hand holds is what comes out. spells is by what a hand holds, and by what both hold (either order) when both make the same gesture; a gesture with no such row, like every sweep today, leaves each hand to its own, as different gestures do. A row is a spell, or an act for a hand with no spell. A hand's buttons, and the other hand's, come together inside window ticks of the first press, which a spell's cast holds open. range is how far a gesture's spell lands, in cells, by rangeOf. A spell's cooldown is handCooldown ticks on its hand, bothCooldown on both for a combined one. kit is the D-pad's list during a run.",
